//@version=6
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ICT STRUCTURE TOOLKIT (IST) · v0.9.1-dev · LRL + HTF fair value gaps + CISD + displacement + IFVG development build
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  Baseline        Phase 1 = v0.3.2 (git tag PHASE1_BASELINE_v0.3.2). Phase 1
//                  behaviour is unchanged; Phase 2 is an additional module.
//  Scope           Phase 1: FVG engine · PDH/PDL · PWH/PWL · sessions · FVG alerts
//                  Phase 2: swings · BSL/SSL · taken · sweep vs break · EQH/EQL
//                  (DEF-L1…L7 → docs/LIQUIDITY.md) · debug
//                  LRL: diagonal failure-swing liquidity, detection only
//                  (DEF-LRL1…LRL8 → docs/LRL.md). Phase 2 frozen baseline =
//                  v0.4.4-dev (tag PHASE2_BASELINE_v0.4.4-dev); LRL is additive.
//                  HTF FVG: fair value gaps of the 15m / 30m / 1H / 4H / 1D / 1W
//                  candles (DEF-B0…B6 → docs/HTF_FVG.md); additive, Module B.
//                  CISD: change in state of delivery, detection only (CISD-R,
//                  DEF-CISD1…CISD9 → docs/CISD.md); additive, reads bars only.
//                  Displacement: one closed candle that reprices aggressively, detection
//                  only (DISPLACEMENT-R, DEF-DISP1…DISP9 → docs/DISPLACEMENT.md); additive,
//                  reads bars only, no state machine, no renderer and no alert yet.
//                  IFVG: inversion fair value gaps (IFVG-R, DEF-IFVG1…IFVG9 →
//                  docs/IFVG.md); an observer of the frozen Phase 1 FVG engine (it
//                  never writes it); additive, no renderer and no alert yet.
//  Layers          L1 market data / time   L2 detection   L3 state management
//                  L4 context / filtering  L5 event bus   L6 renderer
//                  L7 alerts / diagnostics
//  Core rules      · Calculation never depends on visibility. L3 reads no display
//                    input; L6 reads state and never writes it (only the drawing
//                    handles stored on records).
//                  · Logical deletion is deliberate: only the engine-memory policy
//                    removes an FVG record, and it logs FVG_DROPPED_MEMORY.
//                  · Ids are times (FVG: candle-3 time, session: start time), so
//                    they survive reloads that move the first loaded bar.
//  Repaint         Default: state changes once per bar, at the close. HTF values
//                  use expr[1] + lookahead_on = the previous *completed* HTF bar.
//  Definitions     DEF-xx → docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, Appendix A.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("ICT Structure Toolkit", shorttitle = "IST", overlay = true,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ════ ENUMS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

enum MitRule
    firstTouch   = "First touch"
    midpoint     = "Midpoint (CE)"
    fullFill     = "Full fill"
    closeThrough = "Close through"

enum MitView
    remove = "Remove"
    fade   = "Fade"

enum ZoneAnchor
    origin  = "Candle 1 (origin)"
    confirm = "Candle 3 (confirmation)"

enum AlertTiming
    barClose = "Bar close"
    intrabar = "Intrabar (experimental)"

enum LblSize
    tiny   = "Tiny"
    small  = "Small"
    normal = "Normal"

enum LnStyle
    solid  = "Solid"
    dashed = "Dashed"
    dotted = "Dotted"

enum LiqPreset
    aggressive = "Aggressive"
    balanced   = "Balanced"
    strict     = "Strict"
    custom     = "Custom"

enum LiqAnchor
    origin  = "Swing bar (origin)"
    confirm = "Confirmation bar"

// ════ INPUTS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

G_GEN  = "GENERAL"
G_FVGC = "FVG · CALCULATION"
G_FVGV = "FVG · DISPLAY"
G_LVL  = "LEVELS · DISPLAY"
G_SES  = "SESSIONS"
G_ALR  = "ALERTS"
G_DBG  = "DEVELOPER"
G_LIQC = "LIQUIDITY · CALCULATION"
G_LIQV = "LIQUIDITY · DISPLAY"
G_EQ   = "EQH / EQL"
G_LRL  = "LRL · DIAGONAL LIQUIDITY"
G_HTF  = "HTF FAIR VALUE GAPS"
G_CISD = "CISD · CHANGE IN STATE OF DELIVERY"
G_DISP = "DISPLACEMENT"
G_IFVG = "IFVG · INVERSION FAIR VALUE GAPS"

TT_CONF = "[calc] ON: every state change is evaluated once, at bar close. Realtime output is identical to the historical chart after reload.\nOFF (live): wick milestones update intrabar. Creation and invalidation still wait for the close."
TT_MIN  = "[view] Hides secondary visuals: CE lines, FVG labels, faded FVGs, session boxes and midpoints, taken liquidity levels and liquidity labels."
TT_TRA  = "[calc] Gap ≥ k × TR average. TR average = simple (unweighted) mean of the true range of the len bars ending at candle 1 (t-2). Deliberately NOT Wilder ATR. Known at candle 1's close; never changes afterwards. 0 = off."
TT_RNG  = "[calc] Gap ≥ k × average (high − low) of the len bars ending at candle 1 (t-2). Known at candle 1's close. 0 = off."
TT_MEM  = "[calc] FVG records kept per direction, open and closed. Over the limit, the oldest CLOSED (invalidated) record goes first, then the oldest open one. Each removal logs FVG_DROPPED_MEMORY. Lifecycle history older than this window is not available."
TT_MIT  = "[view/alert] When a zone stops being displayed as active (fades or disappears). The engine records first touch, CE, full fill and invalidation independently, whatever this is set to."
TT_ANC  = "[view] Where a zone's box starts. Candle 3 (default) = where it became known, so nothing is drawn before confirmation. Candle 1 = where the imbalance sits (ICT convention; optional). Either way the FVG exists only from candle 3's close."
TT_PREV = "[view] Provisional, CAN REPAINT. Draws the gap the unfinished candle would create if it closed now. Dashed, never stored, never logged, never alerted. Live mode only."
TT_ANCH = "[view] ON: line starts at the bar that printed the extreme, when that is verifiable from loaded bars. Otherwise it starts where the level became known (period start)."
TT_SES  = "[calc] IANA timezone for session windows and the midnight open (DST handled by TradingView). Session windows are [calc]; every other setting in this group is [view]. Hidden sessions are still tracked."
TT_ALT  = "[alert] Bar close: one message per bar, at the close, listing that bar's events.\nIntrabar (experimental): each event fires once, the moment it is logged. Needs Confirmed only = OFF. Close-dependent events still fire at the close.\nCreate the alert with condition 'Any alert() function call'."
TT_LPRE = "[calc] Each preset is four fixed numbers, nothing else:\nAggressive · left 3 · right 2 · reaction ≥ 0.5 × TR average · dominance 10 bars\nBalanced · left 5 · right 3 · reaction ≥ 1.0 × TR average · dominance 30 bars\nStrict · left 10 · right 5 · reaction ≥ 2.0 × TR average · dominance 60 bars\nCustom · the three inputs below, no dominance.\nDominance: no high above the swing high + EQ tolerance in the W bars before the swing bar (lows mirrored)."
TT_LWIN = "[calc] Custom only. Swing high at bar X: its high is above every high of the `left` bars before X and at or above every high of the `right` bars after X (swing low mirrored). It is known only when bar X + right closes: that bar is its confirmation."
TT_LREA = "[calc] Custom only. Reaction = how far price moved away from the swing during the `right` confirmation bars (swing high − lowest low of those bars; mirrored for lows), in multiples of the TR average (14) at the swing bar. 0 = every confirmed swing becomes liquidity."
TT_LMEM = "[calc] Liquidity records kept per side (BSL, SSL), active and taken. Over the limit, the oldest closed taken record goes first, then the oldest live one. Each removal logs BSL/SSL_DROPPED_MEMORY."
TT_LANC = "[view] Where a level's line starts. Confirmation bar (default) = where it became known, so nothing is drawn before it existed. Swing bar = where the extreme printed (optional). Either way the level exists only from the confirmation bar's close."
TT_LTKN = "[view] Taken levels: a faded dotted line ending at the bar that took the level, tagged sweep or break. Newest first, capped per side."
TT_EQT  = "[calc] Swings of the same side whose prices differ by at most this many ticks are 'equal'. 0 = identical prices only."
TT_EQM  = "[calc] Swings needed before a cluster counts as EQH/EQL and EQH/EQL_CREATED is logged."
TT_LRL  = "[calc] LRL = a diagonal line through three or more successive failure swings: descending swing highs (bearish LRL, buy stops above) or ascending swing lows (bullish LRL). Fixed definition, no tuning inputs (docs/LRL.md): pivots left 3 · right 2 · consecutive points at most 30 bars apart, each beyond the EQ tolerance from the previous one and separated by a pullback ≥ 1.0 × TR average · tolerance τ = max(EQ tolerance, 0.5 × TR average at the first point) · the line through the first and the latest point, every point within τ of it, no high above it + τ, total drop > 2τ. Two points are only an internal candidate. Decided at bar close. OFF: nothing is computed; Phase 1 and Phase 2 output is the same either way."
TT_LRLS = "[view] The nearest active LRL per side: one thin straight line from its first to its latest failure swing (the intermediate swings lie within τ of it), the same line dashed to the right while it is active, and a small LRL label. When a later swing extends the LRL, the line is redrawn first → new latest from that bar on."
TT_LRLH = "[view] Also draw ended LRLs (the last 10 per side), faded; the projection ends on the bar where the LRL ended."
TT_LRLM = "[view] Where an ended LRL finished: D drift (the high crossed the projected boundary but not the boundary projected on the previous bar) · S sweep · B break (closed beyond the boundary) · E expired. Needs Show historical LRL."
TT_CISD  = "[calc] CISD = change in state of delivery (docs/CISD.md, CISD-R; no tuning inputs). Bullish: the level L is the OPEN of the first candle of the down-close series that delivered price into the lowest down-close low of the current down leg (only down-close candles count; a doji ends a series; an equal low moves L to the later series). The CISD is the first close strictly above L (a wick, or a close exactly at L, is not; any candle colour). Bearish is the exact mirror. The state of delivery starts UNKNOWN, and bullish and bearish CISDs then strictly alternate. Decided at bar close. OFF: nothing is computed; every other module's output is the same either way."
TT_CISDS = "[view] The current CISD only: a short 1 px line at L, from the first candle of the delivery series to the confirming candle, and a small CISD label. A CISD confirmed in the first 200 loaded bars is never drawn (chart-start guard; it is still part of the logical state)."
TT_DISP  = "[calc] Displacement (docs/DISPLACEMENT.md, DISPLACEMENT-R; no tuning inputs): one closed candle that reprices aggressively. Bullish: close above the open, body ≥ 1.5 × A (A = the TR average of the 14 closed bars before the candle), close in the top quarter of the candle's range, close above the previous candle's high. Bearish is the exact mirror. Decided at the candle's close; a historical fact (no lifecycle). Whether the candle left a fair value gap (candle 2 of a Phase 1 FVG) is recorded on the next bar as metadata only. No drawing or alert yet (Debug mode and Pine Logs show it). OFF: nothing is computed; every other module's output is the same either way."
TT_IFVG  = "[calc] IFVG = inversion fair value gap (docs/IFVG.md, IFVG-R; no tuning inputs). A Phase 1 FVG that a candle closes strictly beyond (its existing invalidation: a bullish FVG's close below its bottom, a bearish FVG's close above its top) becomes an IFVG of the opposite side, with exactly the same top, bottom and CE, at that candle's close. From the next bar: first touch (retest), CE, full traversal; it ends on a close strictly beyond its far edge. It follows the Phase 1 FVG settings (which FVGs exist), never the FVG display. No drawing or alert yet (Debug mode and Pine Logs show it). OFF: nothing is computed; every other module's output is the same either way."
TT_HTF  = "[view] Fair value gaps of the 15m, 30m, 1H, 4H, 1D and 1W candles (docs/HTF_FVG.md). Every timeframe above the chart timeframe is always computed; these switches only show or hide. Per timeframe: the nearest open zone above and below price. A zone exists from the first chart bar after its third HTF candle closed (no repaint); its box starts at its first HTF candle. Phase 1 FVG definition and thresholds; invalidated only by a close of its own timeframe; no longer drawn once fully filled."

confirmedOnly = input.bool(true, "Confirmed only", tooltip = TT_CONF, group = G_GEN, display = display.none)
minimalMode   = input.bool(false, "Minimal mode", tooltip = TT_MIN, group = G_GEN, display = display.none)
lblSizeIn     = input.enum(LblSize.small, "Label size", group = G_GEN, display = display.none)
rightOffset   = input.int(8, "Right extension (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = G_GEN, display = display.none)

fvgMinTicks = input.int(2, "Min size · ticks", minval = 1, tooltip = "[calc] Gap ≥ n × syminfo.mintick.", group = G_FVGC, display = display.none)
fvgMinTra   = input.float(0.10, "Min size · × TR average", minval = 0, step = 0.05, tooltip = TT_TRA, group = G_FVGC, display = display.none)
fvgMinRng   = input.float(0.0, "Min size · × avg range", minval = 0, step = 0.05, tooltip = TT_RNG, group = G_FVGC, display = display.none)
fvgLen      = input.int(14, "TR-average / avg-range length", minval = 2, tooltip = "[calc] Window length (bars) of both references.", group = G_FVGC, display = display.none)
fvgMemory   = input.int(50, "Engine memory · records per direction", minval = 10, maxval = 200, tooltip = TT_MEM, group = G_FVGC, display = display.none)

fvgShow     = input.bool(false, "Show FVGs", tooltip = "[view] Chart-timeframe FVGs (Phase 1 engine). OFF by default since v0.6.0-dev: the user-facing zones are the HTF FVGs. Calculation, lifecycle, events and alerts are unchanged either way.", group = G_FVGV, display = display.none)
fvgBullCol  = input.color(color.new(#089981, 80), "Bullish", inline = "fc", group = G_FVGV, display = display.none)
fvgBearCol  = input.color(color.new(#F23645, 80), "Bearish", inline = "fc", group = G_FVGV, display = display.none)
